%=SNX 2.02 IGN 25:286:44586 IGN 94:002:00000 25:075:00000 P  9402 2 S
+FILE/COMMENT
 
 IGc20 reference frame: the IGS realization of ITRF2020-u2024
 ============================================================
 
 Station selection:
   IGc20 is a subset of 346 stable, well-performing IGS stations from the 2024
   update of ITRF2020, ITRF2020-u2024. Compared to the previous IGb20 reference
   frame, IGc20 contains 3 new stations, in areas previously sparsely covered
   by IGS reference frame stations: CASC (Cascais, Portugal), MANA (Managua,
   Nicaragua) and MAYG (Dzaoudzi, Mayotte).
 
 Consistency with ground antenna calibrations:
   The IGc20 (= ITRF2020-u2024) station coordinates are consistent with the
   ground antenna calibrations compiled in igs20.atx:
   https://files.igs.org/pub/station/general/igs20.atx.
 
 Transformation parameters:
   ITRF2020-u2024 is aligned in origin, scale and orientation to ITRF2020. The
   transformation parameters between ITRF2020, IGS20, ITRF2020-u2024 and IGc20
   are therefore all zero. The transformation parameters between ITRF2020 /
   IGS20 / ITRF2020-u2024 / IGc20 and past ITRF realizations can be found at:
   https://itrf.ign.fr/docs/solutions/itrf2020/Transfo-ITRF2020_TRFs.txt
 
 Discontinuities:
   IGc20 station coordinates are generally represented by piecewise linear
   functions, i.e., several position+velocity sets valid over successive time
   intervals. Each set is denoted by a solution number (soln) whose validity
   period is given in:
   ftp://igs-rf.ign.fr/pub/IGc20/soln_IGc20.snx
   The discontinuity list in soln_IGc20.snx is based on the ITRF2020-u2024
   discontinuity list but also includes recent discontinuities and will be
   continuously updated as new breaks occur. Because IGc20 does not contain
   coordinates for solns starting after 15 March 2025 (end of ITRF2020-u2024
   input data), stations affected by such recent discontinuities cannot be used
   as reference frame stations anymore.
 
 Post-seismic deformation models:
   The reference coordinates of some IGc20 stations include post-seismic
   deformation models in the form of exponential and/or logarithmic functions.
   These models are given in:
   ftp://igs-rf.ign.fr/pub/IGc20/psd_IGc20.snx
   Details on their application can be found at:
   https://itrf.ign.fr/ftp/pub/itrf/itrf2020/ITRF2020-PSD-model-eqs-IGN.pdf
   The IGc20 positions+velocities of the affected stations cannot be used
   without the post-seismic deformation models.
 
 Seasonal terms:
   While coefficients of annual and semi-annual station displacements were
   provided with ITRF2020-u2024, it was agreed among IGS ACs not to implement
   these seasonal terms for the time being. IGc20 is thus provided without
   seasonal terms. Users wishing to experiment with the ITRF2020-u2024 seasonal
   terms may nevertheless add them to the IGc20 piecewise linear coordinates +
   post-seismic deformation models.
 
 IGc20 core network:
   For the purpose of aligning global GNSS solutions to IGc20, a well-
   distributed sub-network of IGc20 stations, called IGc20 core network, was
   designed. It is composed of 55 clusters of stations (i.e., 55 primary
   stations, each with possible substitutes) selected to ensure a homogeneous
   global distribution and the best possible temporal stability of the core
   network. The list of IGc20 core stations can be found at:
   ftp://igs-rf.ign.fr/pub/IGc20/IGc20_core.txt
 
